  dialogueText: 'Here''s an interesting one.

    In Ilokano, ''agbalin'' means ''become.''

    It
    describes a change from one state or condition into another.

    For example,
    with practice, you can become more confident in speaking Ilokano.

    Listen
    carefully: agbalin.

    Now, try saying ''agbalin'' yourself."

'
